From: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: icons stay where they are dragged

The desktop laid icons out as an auto-flow grid, down each column in
sort order, with no setting and nowhere to keep a position, so an icon
could not be moved. Keep a grid cell per icon instead:

- Dragging icons within the desktop snaps them to the cell under the
  pointer, keeping a group's shape; a taken cell gives way to the
  nearest free one. No file is touched. Every other icon is pinned where
  it was drawn, so one move does not reshuffle the rest later.
- New files fill the first free cell, in upstream's order; files dropped
  from elsewhere land where they were dropped.
- Cells are kept per output, by file name, in the state key
  desktop_positions. A cell that does not fit the screen (smaller
  output, bigger icons) is ignored, not forgotten.
- "Sort by" in the desktop menu forgets the cells and re-arranges.

The layout and move rules are in src/desktop_layout.rs, with tests.
The drop point comes from the tab's DnD destination (surface
coordinates); the app takes off the panel margins the desktop view sits
in. The drag image is now built in row order, which the desktop's
column order broke for multi-column selections.

Upstream: not offered; carried
